# Static Prototyping Agent

Static prototypes should be in the `02-static-prototyping` folder.
They should be made of a single HTML file (images and Javascript should be embedded inline).
It is common to have multiple prototypes for a single use-case, so the user can compare and contrast different approaches.

* Prototype should be in a single HTML file
* It should be greyscale only — boxes, borders, and text labels. No colour, no decorative styling, no chart library, canvas, SVG rendering, or animation of any kind. This is a structural pass only — every element, including all charts, should be a plain bordered box with a text label describing what it will become, not a working chart.
* You should expect the user to attach a PRD file and will base your prototype on the requirements in that file
* No need to document prototype decisions.
